    "body": "This looks to me as if there was an oversight in previous PRs. You can see that the comment above the block says \"We will avoid to add multiple instances of the starship function and keep other user functions if any,\" but the code clearly doesn't do this correctly if `starship_cmd` is in the middle of `$PROMPT_COMMAND`.\r\n\r\nMy guess is that when I tested #1185, I only did so with `.bashrc`s that appended starship without appending other shell frameworks, so I missed the fact that the checking hadn't been changed to update the fact that `starship_precmd` could now appear anywhere in the shell.",
